From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: session-worker: Close a reauthentication's session when its request goes

A reauthentication request held its GdmSession, and so did every
conversation the session started. When the client went away - its
connection closed, or a new request from the same process replaced the
old one - the request dropped its reference and nothing stopped the
conversations: a gdm-password worker waiting for a password kept the
session, and the session its two D-Bus servers and the worker's
connection, for good. Measured on a laptop that woke from suspend every
half minute to show its lock screen: 202 gdm-password workers and 824
files in the session's worker an hour after boot; at 1024 the lock
screen showed no prompt.

The request now closes its session, stopping the conversations, before
it lets it go.

--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
@@ -3358,6 +3358,9 @@
         g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (request->session,
                                               G_CALLBACK (on_reauthentication_verification_complete),
                                               request);
+        /* Each conversation holds the session: stopped, they let it go with its servers and
+         * workers, or a request the client left with services running stays for good. */
+        gdm_session_close (request->session);
         g_clear_object (&request->session);
         g_slice_free (ReauthenticationRequest, request);
 }
